      "issue_dependencies_summary": { "blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0 },
      "body": "Relocated from dezren39/nix#819 on 2026-10-28 (placement audit): mcpx's single source lives in developing-today/code (pkgs/mcpx); re-home tracked at #309. Original body below; issue references inside it are historical (dezren39/nix numbering).\n\n## Problem\n\nmcpx sends no workspace information when it initializes a server: no `rootUri`, no `workspaceFolders` (grep across `internal/mcpclient` and `internal/pool` — none). Workspace-oriented servers therefore start without a workspace session even when mcpx knows exactly which repo the caller is in.\n\nConcrete evidence (live fleet, 2026-10-25): gopls behind mcpx works file-by-file — its file-argument tools load the file ad hoc as a \"command-line-arguments\" package — but it is not a module workspace session: `go_package_api` on a module path returned **empty after 156 s**. Two missing pieces combine here: the process cwd is static (the spawn-cwd issue), and the initialize handshake carries no root even if the cwd were right.\n\n## Proposed design\n\nWhen mcpx has a scope-resolved root for an instance (repo/worktree scope resolution already computes it), include it in the initialize params for that server instance:\n\n- `rootUri` set to the resolved root, and\n- `workspaceFolders` containing that root,\n\nfor servers that declare workspace support in their initialize negotiation. Servers that don't advertise/accept it must be unaffected (send only what the negotiated protocol version and server capabilities allow).\n\nThis is step 3 of the 2026-10-25 per-project design note. It builds on the spawn-cwd issue #817, which introduces the resolved-root plumbing this issue reuses; the `${mcpx.root}` substitution issue #818 is the config-level companion. Order: spawn-cwd/substitution first, this after — flipping gopls to `\"scope\": \"worktree\"` only becomes fully effective once the workspace reaches the server both via cwd *and* via initialize.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] For an instance with a scope-resolved root, the initialize request mcpx sends includes `rootUri`/`workspaceFolders` naming that root (demonstrated by a captured handshake or a test double server that records initialize params).\n- [ ] Servers that don't negotiate workspace support initialize exactly as before.\n- [ ] `global`-scoped instances (no resolved root) send no rootUri/workspaceFolders — no fabricated daemon-cwd root.\n- [ ] With gopls at `\"scope\": \"worktree\"` behind the fixed spawn cwd, `go_package_api` on a module path returns the module's API promptly (the 156 s empty result does not recur).\n- [ ] Tests cover: root present for repo/worktree scopes, absent for global scope.\n",
