      "body": "Slice 3 of decision record 0004 (`pkgs/mcpx/docs/decisions/0004-scope-resolved-roots.md`, PR #957). Design source: dezren39/nix#819 — this issue carries its acceptance criteria. Depends on slice 1 (ResolvedScope plumbing).\n\n## What to build (spec §5)\n- `mcpclient.Options` gains the instance root; when non-empty, initialize for that instance includes `rootUri` (file:// URI of the root), `workspaceFolders` ([{uri, name = base name of root}]), and declares the `workspace.workspaceFolders` client capability true.\n- Both fields are sent for every era (legacy and modern) — initialize params are extensible and non-consuming servers ignore them. When the root is empty, initialize is byte-for-byte what it is today.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (from nix#819, verbatim intent)\n- [ ] For an instance with a scope-resolved root, the initialize request includes `rootUri`/`workspaceFolders` naming that root (demonstrated by a captured handshake or a test-double server recording initialize params).\n- [ ] Servers that don't negotiate workspace support initialize exactly as before.\n- [ ] `global`-scoped instances send no rootUri/workspaceFolders — no fabricated daemon-cwd root.\n- [ ] Tests cover: root present for repo/worktree scopes, absent for global scope.\n\n(The live gopls `go_package_api` proof is slice 4's acceptance.)",
