      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "sub_issues_summary": { "total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0 },
      "issue_dependencies_summary": { "blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0 },
      "body": "Relocated from dezren39/nix#817 on 2026-10-28 (placement audit): mcpx's single source lives in developing-today/code (pkgs/mcpx); re-home tracked at #309. Original body below; issue references inside it are historical (dezren39/nix numbering).\n\n## Problem\n\nmcpx scopes choose *which* process serves a caller, but nothing tells that process *where the caller is*.\n\nScope keys already resolve the caller's cwd to a git root: `internal/config/scope.go` (`CallContext`, `Scope.Key()`) yields `repo:<git-common-dir>` / `worktree:<top-level>` using the native git discovery in `internal/config/gitdiscover.go`. But instance spawn ignores that resolution: `internal/pool/pool.go` `dial()` builds `StdioOptions{Cwd: p.cfg.Cwd}` — the config's static string, verbatim — and `internal/mcpclient/stdio.go` sets `cmd.Dir = opts.Cwd`. A `repo`- or `worktree`-scoped server therefore still *runs* in the daemon's cwd.\n\nConcrete casualty (observed live, 2026-10-25, fleet config of 16 servers): gopls is a workspace server whose workspace is its process cwd. Scoped per-checkout it would still run in the daemon's cwd, so it loads files ad hoc (\"command-line-arguments\" package) instead of as a module workspace session.\n\n## Proposed smallest design\n\nWhen a server's scope is `repo` or `worktree` **and** its config `cwd` is empty, spawn the instance with `Dir` = the resolved scope root (the common-dir's worktree / the checkout top-level) instead of the daemon's cwd.\n\nThis needs the scope resolution to hand the pool the root, not just the opaque key string: return the resolved root alongside the key from `Scope.Key()`, or recompute it via `locateGit` at spawn time. One branch in `pool.dial()`.\n\nExplicit config `cwd` always wins — the scope root is only the default when `cwd` is unset.\n\n## Why this order\n\nThis is step 1 of the per-project design note (2026-10-25). With it, `\"mcpx\": {\"scope\": \"worktree\"}` on gopls becomes a real per-project workspace server: one gopls per checkout, rooted in that checkout. Flipping scopes *before* this lands only multiplies processes for little gain, so config scope flips wait for this issue.\n\nRelated: #818 — the `${mcpx.root}` / `${mcpx.cwd}` substitution issue (companion, step 2) — and #819 — the initialize `rootUri`/`workspaceFolders` issue (step 3, builds on the root resolution here).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A `worktree`-scoped server with no config `cwd` is spawned with its working directory set to the caller's checkout top-level; a `repo`-scoped one to the resolved worktree of the common dir.\n- [ ] Two callers in different checkouts of the same repo get distinct `worktree`-scoped instances rooted in their own checkouts; `repo` scope keeps sharing one instance per common dir.\n- [ ] An explicit config `cwd` overrides the scope root in all cases.\n- [ ] `global`/`cwd:`/`session` and other scopes are unchanged.\n- [ ] A `worktree`-scoped gopls answers a package-level query (e.g. `go_package_api` on a module path) with the module's real API instead of an empty result.\n- [ ] Tests cover the spawn-cwd decision (scope root vs explicit cwd vs daemon cwd fallback).\n",
